title: Las dos Españas
new-page: true
is-special: true
on-arrival: {!
// --- The Two Spains board (Area O D-3): derive the polarization state ---------
// Poder Popular / Poder Institucional (mirrors status.scene.dry).
Q.movement_power = Math.round(
    (Q.ugt_militia_strength + Q.cnt_militia_strength) / 50
    + Q.dues * 2 + (Q.works_councils || 0) * 3 + (Q.radicalization || 0) * 2
    + (Q.nationalization_progress || 0) * 4 + (Q.anarchist_strength || 0) * 0.2
    + (Q.movement_power_bonus || 0));
if (Q.movement_power < 0) Q.movement_power = 0;
Q.institutional_power = Math.round(
    (Q.psoe_in_government ? 15 : 0) + Q.army_loyalty * 30 + Q.asalto_loyalty * 15
    + Q.guardia_civil_loyalty * 10 + Q.budget + (Q.democratization || 0) * 2
    + (Q.welfare || 0) + (Q.institutional_power_bonus || 0));
if (Q.institutional_power < 0) Q.institutional_power = 0;

// Polarization: confrontation signals minus conciliation (mirrored in the crisis
// resolver, events/july_1936_coup, and scripts/balance_sim.mjs).
Q.polarization = Math.round(
    (Q.coup_progress || 0) * 3.5
    + (Q.clerical_conflict || 0) * 2
    + (Q.radicalization || 0) * 1.5
    + (Q.anarchist_insurrection ? 8 : 0)
    + (Q.polarization_bonus || 0)
    - (Q.democratization || 0) * 1.5);
if (Q.polarization < 0) Q.polarization = 0;
if (Q.polarization > 100) Q.polarization = 100;

// Balance of power: the workers'/Popular-Front bloc vs the National/military bloc,
// from the same force components the coup resolver uses. 50 = even.
var left_bloc = Q.ugt_militia_strength * Q.ugt_militia_militancy
    + Q.cnt_militia_strength * Q.cnt_militia_militancy
    + Q.asalto_strength * Q.asalto_loyalty
    + Q.army_strength * Q.army_loyalty;
var right_bloc = Q.falange_militia_strength * Q.falange_militia_militancy
    + Q.requetes_strength * Q.requetes_militancy
    + (Q.africa_army || 0) * 35
    + Q.army_strength * (1 - Q.army_loyalty)
    + Q.guardia_civil_strength * (1 - Q.guardia_civil_loyalty);
Q.balance_of_power = Math.round(100 * left_bloc / (left_bloc + right_bloc + 0.0001));
if (Q.balance_of_power < 0) Q.balance_of_power = 0;
if (Q.balance_of_power > 100) Q.balance_of_power = 100;
!}

= Las dos Españas

Spain is coming apart into two camps that no longer share common ground. Where each finds its power, and how far the rupture has gone, will decide what July 1936 becomes.

**Polarization — the distance between the two Spains:** [+ polarization : polarization +]
[? if polarization < 30 : The Republic still commands a broad centre; compromise is still a language people speak. ?][? if polarization >= 30 and polarization < 60 : The centre is thinning. Each crisis pushes more people to one pole or the other. ?][? if polarization >= 60 and polarization < 85 : There are now two Spains, arming and watching each other; an election settles nothing. ?][? if polarization >= 85 : The country is a powder keg. Any spark will do. ?]

**Balance of power:** [+ balance_of_power +] / 100 [? if balance_of_power >= 55 : — the workers' and republican bloc holds the advantage. ?][? if balance_of_power < 55 and balance_of_power > 45 : — the two camps are evenly matched. ?][? if balance_of_power <= 45 : — the military and the authoritarian right hold the advantage. ?]

<span style="color: #c00000;">Poder Popular</span> (movement / militias / street): [+ movement_power +] &nbsp; | &nbsp; <span style="color: #2E3B6E;">Poder Institucional</span> (ministries / army / law): [+ institutional_power +]

Party line: [+ party_line : party_line +]

<h1>The Military Conspiracy</h1>

Across the barracks of the peninsula and the Army of Africa, a conspiracy against the Republic is taking shape. Its threads run through monarchist salons, Carlist Navarre, and the officers' messes of the Moroccan Protectorate.

Coup preparations: [+ coup_progress : coup_readiness +]

Army of Africa mobilization: [+ africa_army +] — the Legion and the Regulares, the most battle-hardened and least reliable units in the Republic's service.

Peninsular Army (strength [+ army_strength +] thousand) loyalty: [+ army_loyalty : loyalty +]

<h1>The Plotters</h1>

<span style="font-weight: bold;">General Emilio Mola</span> — "El Director." From his posting in Pamplona he coordinates the rising, drafting the secret instructions that would bind the scattered garrisons, the Carlist Requetés, and the Falange into a single plan.

<span style="font-weight: bold;">General José Sanjurjo</span> — the figurehead, exiled in Portugal since his failed 1932 *pronunciamiento*. The plotters intend to fly him home to head the new regime.

<span style="font-weight: bold;">General Francisco Franco</span> — cautious and the last to commit, but commander of the Canaries garrison and the officer the Africanistas trust to lead the Army of Africa across the Strait.

<span style="font-weight: bold;">General Manuel Goded</span> — marked to seize Barcelona and Catalonia for the rising.

<span style="font-weight: bold;">General Gonzalo Queipo de Llano</span> — the unpredictable Africanista who will move on Seville and the south.

<h1>The Civilian Front</h1>

José Calvo Sotelo's monarchists give the conspiracy its parliamentary voice; the Falange of José Antonio Primo de Rivera and the Carlist Requetés of Navarre supply its street militias and shock troops.
